Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:09:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: silent nn::audio, nn::time, nested guest
 calls, NVN submit bookkeeping, frame dump, hang reports

nn::audio client API replaced by host bookkeeping (voices consume wave buffers at the sample rate, pools attach at once, the renderer event ticks every sampleCount/sampleRate, audio-out buffers release after their duration); nn::time over the host clocks; Horizon.call_guest runs guest code from a service handler (the SDK's own CreateSystemEvent); nvnCommandBufferGetCommandMemoryUsed so the game submits what it recorded; NX2LINUX_DUMP_FRAME writes PNGs of presented frames; the runner reports where every guest thread waits and the clear colours. Found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: S7bis: silent audio, time, first frames presented by Xenoblade Chronicles 2, and AOT runtime fixes found doing it; tests use synthetic code and fake guest memory, no game data
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

